/-!
# M14 canonical society / UBI whole-program sink

A canonical society is not a terminal state.  This fixed flagship instance
has no source-free identity, renews rather than eternalizes institutional
power, accounts for the payment residual and its consumer, denies observer
readouts legislative authority, preserves actionable exit after employment
loss, and carries an actual self-U8 path on the same old root as the UBI
source program.

UBI is characterized here at maximum fixed-instance strength: one exact
periodic source-backed payment becomes actionable exit iff an uncaptured,
non-idle independent continuation has its exact payment receipt, generated
crossing route, and actual debited service slot.  Nominal transfer, full price
capture, role-dependent job standing, and anomie are independently separated.
-/

